{"assumptions":["ASM-1 (high risk): invoices, customers, the invoice status and the customer email field already exist in the client's .NET 8 API and Postgres database and are read from there. No repository was available, so every requirement is ADDED and all endpoint paths and field names (e.g. GET /api/overdue-invoices or /api/invoices/overdue, GET /api/invoices/{id}, POST /api/invoices/{id}/reminders) are placeholders to be mapped to the real API.","Invoice status (fixes the REQ-2 finding): current behaviour has no claims, so the real status values are unknown. An invoice can only be overdue if it has the one status meaning 'open / unpaid, issued to the customer'. Any other status (paid, closed, void, cancelled, draft, written off, or anything else) and any invoice with no due date is left out. The client must confirm how its real status values map to 'open'.","Days-overdue buckets: ASM-5 (7–30/31–60/61–90/90+) is used over ASM-14 (7–14/15–30/30+), with the top bucket starting at 91 so buckets don't overlap. The client must confirm.","Email channel: ASM-6 (transactional provider) is used over ASM-12 (existing SMTP relay), because Q-8 needs bounces reported back and a plain SMTP relay can't reliably do that. The client must confirm before run 3 (bounce webhook).","Email template (applies to run 2): the wording and from address come from a configured template; ASM-8 (client provides wording) and ASM-15 (we draft, client approves) are combined. The body must contain invoice number, amount and due date.","The overdue threshold is an app setting with default 7 (ASM-3/ASM-10). Today's date comes from a configured business timezone (ASM-9/ASM-11). Days overdue counts whole calendar days from the due date (ASM-4), so an invoice first appears on the list with days overdue = 7.","Send timeout (applies to run 2): there is one budget. The provider call times out after 8 s and the endpoint returns within 10 s (NFR-3). This replaces the earlier conflicting NFR-4 and NFR-5 values.","The double-submit window (applies to run 2) is 60 seconds, checked per invoice on the server (ASM-13), counting from the previous accepted request that reached the provider, whatever the provider outcome. Duplicates rejected this way are not recorded in reminder history.","Requests blocked before any provider call (missing email, not overdue, duplicate, unauthenticated) are not delivery attempts and create no reminder history entry. Q-3's 'every attempt' is read as every attempt that reaches the provider (applies to run 2).","The sender recorded in history (run 2) is the identity of the authenticated user from the existing API authentication.","Error status codes (400, 401, 404, 409, 422, 502) are proposals; the client API's own error conventions take priority if they differ.","Reminder history is returned newest first. Reminders can be sent for any overdue invoice through the send-reminder endpoint (run 2), which both screens will use in run 4 (ASM-16).","Send-reminder button on a non-overdue invoice (fixes the REQ-19/REQ-20 conflict): the drafted REQ-20, which showed the button on every invoice, is dropped. The button only appears for overdue invoices (drafted REQ-19), which matches REQ-10's rejection of sends for invoices that are not overdue. This decision carries into run 4.","Run sequence (fixes the size finding): the feature is split into four runs. Run 1 is the overdue list API (REQ-1–REQ-7), run 2 is reminders, history and invoice detail (REQ-8–REQ-12, REQ-15, REQ-16), run 3 is the bounce webhook (REQ-13, REQ-14), and run 4 is the screens (REQ-17–REQ-19). Requirement IDs stay the same across runs."],"critic":[{"finding":"The overdue threshold can be configured (REQ-1, AC-1.4 sets it to 10), but the bucket bounds are fixed at 7–30/31–60/61–90/91+, so with a threshold of 3 an invoice 3–6 days overdue is on the list but in no bucket, and with 10 the 7–30 bucket's lower bound is wrong.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The bucket boundaries (7, 30, 31, 60, 61, 90, 91) are fixed in the requirement, while the threshold they depend on is a configuration setting (ASM-3/ASM-10), and the two assumptions disagreed on the buckets (ASM-5 vs ASM-14).","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":8,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"NFR-1 and NFR-2 describe the same performance target at two different data sizes (10,000 invoices/1,000 customers vs 5,000 open invoices/500 customers), with unexplained 'd1' and 'd2/d3' labels, so it is unclear which size is the acceptance target.","reqId":"NFR-1","rubric":1,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"REQ-2 and AC-2.1 treat the statuses 'open', paid, closed, void, cancelled, draft and written off as if they exist in the client's invoice data, but the current-behaviour artifact has no claims and no repository was found, so these values have no anchor.","reqId":"REQ-2","rubric":5,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"REQ-4 assumes the existing records have a customer name, an amount and a date-only due date, with no anchor; currency, and whether the due date is stored as a timestamp that needs converting to the business timezone, are not addressed.","reqId":"REQ-4","rubric":5,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Only a valid customer with no overdue invoices is covered (AC-5.2); there is no defined response for a customer filter that doesn't exist or is malformed (404 vs 400 vs empty 200).","reqId":"REQ-5","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"Only unauthenticated or invalid tokens are covered (401); there is no rule for a request that is authenticated under the existing scheme but is not a staff user (e.g. 403), even though access is limited to 'any authenticated staff user'.","reqId":"REQ-7","rubric":2,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"There is no behaviour for an invalid or missing configured threshold (zero, negative, non-numeric) or business timezone, and no AC for an empty overdue list when no filter is applied.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":2,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"Existing records that break the assumed shape are not handled: an open invoice whose customer is missing or deleted (no customer name for REQ-4), or a partly paid invoice that is still 'open'.","reqId":"REQ-1","rubric":6,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"AC-3.1 is checked by comparing raw Postgres rows byte for byte against a snapshot, which is a check on database internals rather than anything visible at the API surface.","reqId":"REQ-3","rubric":3,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"The ACs refer to 'the overdue list endpoint' and to bucket values without fixing the path (the assumptions give two different placeholder paths), the query parameter names or the format of the bucket values (e.g. how '90+' is sent), so a test can't be written against a concrete API contract.","reqId":"REQ-6","rubric":3,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The spec's assumptions narrow the human's Q-3 answer 'Every attempt, each with a delivery status' to 'every attempt that reaches the provider', so blocked sends (missing email, duplicate, not overdue) are excluded from history, which contradicts the accepted answer.","reqId":"REQ-11","rubric":1,"severity":"medium"},{"finding":"This run is limited to REQ-1–REQ-7, but its assumptions fix behaviour for later runs (8 s provider timeout, 60 s double-submit window counted from the previous accepted request, history exclusions, a dropped REQ-20) and say those deferred requirements 'keep their IDs and wording', without that wording being reviewable here.","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":4,"severity":"low"},{"finding":"The 60 s double-submit window and the 8 s provider timeout / 10 s endpoint budget are stated as fixed values rather than configuration, even though ASM-13 offered 60 s only as an example ('e.g. 60s').","reqId":"REQ-15","rubric":8,"severity":"low"}],"lint":[{"check":"L1 ids","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L2 req-ac","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L3 ears","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L4 vague","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L5 nfr","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L6 scope","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L8 anchors","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L9 size","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L10 trace","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L11 observable","details":"ok","passed":true},{"check":"L12 literals","details":"ok","passed":true}],"nfrs":[{"id":"NFR-1","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1000 ms with 10,000 invoices and 1,000 customers in the database, with or without filters","text":"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d1 sizing)."},{"id":"NFR-2","metric":"p95 response time ≤ 1000 ms with 5,000 open invoices and 500 customers","text":"The overdue list endpoint responds quickly at the expected data size, with or without filters (d2/d3 sizing)."}],"outOfScope":["Payments and recording payments or marking invoices paid (invoices leave the list only through the status already in the invoice data)","Customer logins or any customer-facing screens","SMS reminders","Automatic or scheduled reminders that no staff user triggers","Saving or writing an overdue flag/status on invoice records","More than one email address per customer, or choosing a recipient","Role-based permissions beyond 'any authenticated staff user'","Editing the email template from the UI (template is stored in config)","Creating or editing invoices and customer records, including customer email addresses","Deferred to run 2 of this sequence: sending reminders, reminder history and the invoice detail endpoint (I-2, I-3, the send-time part of I-4, and the API behind I-7). This covers drafted REQ-8 (send email via provider), REQ-9 (block when no customer email), REQ-10 (reject when invoice not overdue), REQ-11 (record every provider attempt with sender, timestamp and status), REQ-12 (send-time failures and 8 s timeout), REQ-15 (60 s double-submit block), REQ-16 (invoice detail with reminder history), the 401 check for the invoice detail and send-reminder endpoints (with no email sent and no history row), and NFR-3 (send timeout budget), NFR-8 (reminder audit retention) and NFR-9 (no duplicate sends under concurrency). These keep their IDs and wording.","Deferred to run 3 of this sequence: bounces reported later by the email provider through a signed webhook (the bounce part of I-4/Q-8; drafted as REQ-13, REQ-14 and NFR-6).","Deferred to run 4 of this sequence: the overdue list screen (I-6) and invoice detail screen (I-7) in the React front end (drafted as REQ-17, REQ-18, REQ-19). Run 1 (this run) delivers the overdue list API (REQ-1–REQ-7) and run 2 delivers the reminder and invoice detail API that those screens call."],"requirements":[{"acceptance":[{"given":"threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-08, and an open invoice INV-1 has due date 2026-09-01","id":"AC-1.1","level":"api","then":"the response is 200 and contains INV-1","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"threshold is 7, business timezone is UTC, today is 2026-09-07, and an open invoice INV-2 has due date 2026-09-01 (6 days past due)","id":"AC-1.2","level":"api","then":"the response does not contain INV-2","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"business timezone is UTC+2, the current UTC time is 2026-09-07T23:30Z (local date 2026-09-08), threshold is 7, and an open invoice INV-3 has due date 2026-09-01","id":"AC-1.3","level":"api","then":"the response contains INV-3","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"the overdue threshold setting is changed to 10, today is 2026-10-15, and open invoices are due 2026-10-05 and 2026-10-06","id":"AC-1.4","level":"api","then":"the response contains the invoice due 2026-10-05 and does not contain the invoice due 2026-10-06","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"}],"ears":"When an authenticated staff user requests the overdue list, the invoice reminders API shall return every invoice that has the open status and a due date and for which today's date in the configured business timezone is on or after its due date plus the configured overdue threshold (default 7 days).","id":"REQ-1","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-2","Q-6","ASM-1","ASM-2","ASM-3","ASM-9"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"invoices C (paid), D (closed), E (void) and F (draft) are each 30 days past their due date, and open invoice G has no due date","id":"AC-2.1","level":"api","then":"none of C, D, E, F or G is in the response","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"invoice INV-6 is in the overdue list and its status is then changed to paid or closed in the invoice data","id":"AC-2.2","level":"api","then":"the response no longer contains INV-6, with no other action needed","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called again with a valid staff token"}],"ears":"If an invoice has any status other than open in the existing invoice data (including paid, closed, void, cancelled, draft or written off) or has no due date, then the invoice reminders API shall leave it out of the overdue list.","id":"REQ-2","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","Q-4","ASM-1"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"a snapshot of all invoice rows in Postgres is taken, and some of those invoices are overdue","id":"AC-3.1","level":"api","then":"every invoice row is byte-for-byte unchanged compared with the snapshot (no status or updated-at column written)","when":"the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token, with and without filters"}],"ears":"The invoice reminders API shall work out overdue status at query time without writing any overdue flag or status to invoice records.","id":"REQ-3","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-6","ASM-2"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"today is 2026-10-15 in the business timezone and open invoice INV-100 for customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, is due 2026-10-01","id":"AC-4.1","level":"api","then":"the response's INV-100 entry has invoice number INV-100, customer 'Crumb & Co', amount 250.00, due date 2026-10-01 and days overdue 14","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"},{"given":"today is 2026-09-08, threshold is 7 and open invoice INV-1 is due 2026-09-01","id":"AC-4.2","level":"api","then":"the response's INV-1 entry has days overdue 7","when":"GET the overdue list endpoint is called with a valid staff token"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested, the invoice reminders API shall return, for each overdue invoice, its invoice number, customer name, amount, due date and days overdue, where days overdue is the number of whole calendar days from the due date to today in the business timezone.","id":"REQ-4","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-1","I-6","ASM-4","ASM-9"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"customer A has 2 overdue invoices and customer B has 3 overdue invoices","id":"AC-5.1","level":"api","then":"the response contains exactly customer A's 2 overdue invoices","when":"the overdue list is requested filtered by customer A"},{"given":"customer C has no overdue invoices","id":"AC-5.2","level":"api","then":"the response is 200 with an empty list","when":"the overdue list is requested filtered by customer C"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a customer filter, the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices belonging to that customer.","id":"REQ-5","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"overdue invoices with days overdue 7, 30, 31, 60, 61, 90 and 91","id":"AC-6.1","level":"api","then":"the 7–30 response contains 7 and 30; 31–60 contains 31 and 60; 61–90 contains 61 and 90; 90+ contains only 91","when":"the overdue list is requested with each bucket in turn"},{"given":"customer A has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days and customer B has overdue invoices at 10 and 40 days","id":"AC-6.2","level":"api","then":"the response contains only customer A's 40-day invoice","when":"the overdue list is requested with customer A and bucket 31–60"},{"given":"any data","id":"AC-6.3","level":"api","then":"the response is 400 and names the allowed bucket values","when":"the overdue list is requested with a bucket value that is not one of the four buckets (e.g. 5-9)"}],"ears":"When the overdue list is requested with a days-overdue bucket filter of 7–30, 31–60, 61–90 or 91 and over (90+), the invoice reminders API shall return only overdue invoices whose days overdue falls inside that bucket, bounds included.","id":"REQ-6","op":"ADDED","sources":["I-5","ASM-4","ASM-5"],"stability":1},{"acceptance":[{"given":"no authentication credentials and at least one overdue invoice in the database","id":"AC-7.1","level":"api","then":"each response is 401 with no invoice or customer fields in the body","when":"the overdue list endpoint is called, with and without filters"},{"given":"an expired or invalid staff token and at least one overdue invoice in the database","id":"AC-7.2","level":"api","then":"the response is 401 with no invoice or customer fields in the body","when":"the overdue list endpoint is called"}],"ears":"If a request to the overdue list endpoint has no valid staff authentication under the existing API's authentication scheme, then the invoice reminders API shall reject it with HTTP 401 and return no invoice or customer data.","id":"REQ-7","op":"ADDED","sources":["Q-1"],"stability":1}],"roundTrip":{"droppedSpans":[],"inventedCapabilities":[]}}